results.product:
This is the Hindi/English voice layer of an AI tutor. Lanes:
- a cascade lane: gpt-live-transcribe STT, then a server brain (classify, reply or agent), then Azure Speech DragonHD TTS in framed PCM/ADPCM over a single turn-audio response;
- a premium realtime lane;
- the agent lane: one structured-output LLM call per turn with code-checked actions, behind an owner cohort flag and off in production as of release 14.1;
- duplex modes: D4 (own engine on gpt-live-transcribe, now half-duplex by default) and D5 (Azure AI Voice Live as the ear only: stereo mic plus played-audio reference AEC, DNS, multilingual semantic VAD, hi-IN/en-IN ASR, create_response false), with Taxila's own engine owning the floor.
Everything is built and tested in simulated harnesses and the owner cohort. Nothing is validated on real children or real phones; D5's end-of-turn misses its 900 ms bar (1480 ms) because Voice Live returns empty transcripts on short answers. The bake-off also produced an explicit per-minute cost model for an enterprise voice-calling SaaS on Azure: about $0.027/min AI for Voice Live front end plus cascade vs $0.088 for gpt-realtime.
